<SupportLayout title="Purchase Terms" eyebrow="SUPPORT / PURCHASES" description="How music, merchandise, and event-related purchases are handled when you visit Perennial Fallout online.">
  <h2>1. About purchases on this website</h2>
  <p>Perennial Fallout shares music previews, band information, and show announcements here. Selecting <strong>Buy Track</strong> for “The Way” opens the <a href="https://perennial-fallout-shop.fourthwall.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Perennial Fallout Fourthwall storefront homepage</a>, not a direct product checkout. If the song is listed for sale, select its product page there to view its details and complete a purchase. This website does not collect payment-card details or process checkout itself.</p>
  <p>Review the current product description, total price, payment options, and delivery terms on Fourthwall before placing an order.</p>
  <h2>2. Purchases through third parties</h2>
  <p>Purchases made through the band's <a href="https://perennial-fallout-shop.fourthwall.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fourthwall shop</a> are processed on that external platform. The band may link to independent ticketing, streaming, or merchandise providers in the future. Check the seller and their applicable terms, privacy notice, fees, delivery, and refund rules before paying.</p>
  <h2>3. Music previews and downloads</h2>
  <p>Music available to play on this site is provided for personal listening and promotional purposes. Streaming or playing a preview does not transfer ownership of the sound recording or grant permission to reproduce, distribute, resell, remix, or publicly exploit the music.</p>
  <p>If “The Way” is offered as a digital download on Fourthwall, its product page will specify the available file format (such as MP3) and included content. The band's website provides only a 45-second promotional preview. Copyright in the music and recording remains with the relevant rights holders unless expressly stated otherwise. Buying a download does not grant redistribution, resale, public performance, or commercial licensing rights.</p>
  <h2>4. Pricing, delivery, and availability</h2>
  <p>When a product is available for purchase, Fourthwall displays its current price and any applicable taxes or fees during checkout. For eligible digital orders, Fourthwall provides the order confirmation and emails the download link when the file is ready. Check your spam or junk folder if you do not receive the email. The presence of a shop link on this website does not guarantee a specific song is currently for sale. Other ticket or merchandise sellers have their own pricing and delivery policies.</p>
  <h2>5. Refunds, problems, and cancellations</h2>
  <p>For Fourthwall order, refund, or download issues, use the help options in the order confirmation or contact <a class="support-email" href="mailto:perennialfallout@gmail.com?subject=The%20Way%20Purchase%20Support">perennialfallout@gmail.com</a> with your order reference (not your card details). Refund eligibility is subject to the checkout provider's applicable terms and consumer law. For other third-party sellers, contact the seller using the order receipt.</p>
  <p>If an event is rescheduled or canceled, check the venue or ticket issuer for official information about tickets. Information appearing here is not a guarantee that an event will proceed as listed.</p>
  <h2>6. Questions about an offering</h2>
  <p>For questions about whether a product or download is officially offered by the band, contact <a class="support-email" href="mailto:perennialfallout@gmail.com?subject=Purchase%20Question">perennialfallout@gmail.com</a>. Do not send payment-card details or sensitive financial information by email.</p>
  <div class="support-note"><p><strong>Payment security:</strong> Perennial Fallout does not ask for payment card numbers by email and does not process or store card details on this website. Any purchase and digital delivery of “The Way” through our shop are handled by Fourthwall.</p></div>
</SupportLayout>
